From e8fb7e823032b25fdc218677dbde286ac834c9bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:23:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] layout: render the top layer and ::backdrop

Modal dialogs and open popovers painted inside their ancestors' stacking
contexts, so any z-index above theirs covered them, transformed or clipping
ancestors trapped them, and ::backdrop was never drawn.

The user agent stylesheet now marks dialog:modal, :popover-open and
::backdrop with the internal -servo-top-layer property and gives popovers
their HTML rendering rules. Boxes in the top layer:
- hoist past every containing block to the initial containing block,
- always establish a stacking context,
- are collected at their placeholders and built last on the root stacking
  context, above every other stacking context in top layer order,
- get a ::backdrop box built right before them, so it paints just below.
Entering or leaving the top layer rebuilds the parent's boxes, which own
the ::backdrop sibling. Fullscreen elements, which already used
-servo-top-layer, get Chrome's black backdrop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
